    "done_when": "Done when a new tests/test_a_probe_is_read_for_the_program_it_runs.py shows five things: The §1 probe, verbatim, is accepted as naming job 1306915. [\"python3\",\"-c\",\"print('pending')\"] is still refused, and the refusal contains the sentence that the probe runs the interpreter python3 whose code string names no reference, which today's refusal does not. An interpreter probe running sacct --json -j 1306915 is refused as structured output, as the plain sacct --json probe is. [\"squeue\",\"-h\",\"-j1306915\"] is accepted as naming job 1306915, where today it is refused as a probe that cannot fail. A shell probe's reading is unchanged: [\"bash\",\"-c\",\"squeue -h -j 1274028); echo\"] still names job 1274028. Five negative controls: reading interpreter strings as one token refuses the first case; splitting on the shell's separator set alone refuses the first case; leaving _wait_probe_prints_structured_output on probe[0] accepts the third case; dropping the glued form from the flag rule refuses the fourth case; and today's refusal text fails the second case. The test files importing reckon.crew.recovery_wait or reckon.crew.recovery_liveness add no failure against the base revision, run one arm at a time with at most -n 4 . Ruff adds no findings on the staged paths. Every log is under the run directory, starts with its revision and the literal command, and ends in EXIT= . Write paths: reckon/crew/recovery_wait.py , reckon/crew/recovery_liveness.py and the new test.",
